Procedure Modeling of Building

This repository contains a partial Ruby implementation of "Procedural Modeling of Buildings" by P. Mueller.
Reference paper:
https://peterwonka.net/Publications/pdfs/2006.SG.Mueller.ProceduralModelingOfBuildings.final.pdf


## Build Sprite Atlases

Build atlas from an image directory:
```sh
ruby promobu/dir_sprite_pack.rb nyc1920 --out-dir rules --output-base nyc1920-sprites
ruby promobu/dir_sprite_pack.rb ttd --out-dir rules --output-base ttd-sprites
ruby promobu/dir_sprite_pack.rb canary --out-dir rules --output-base canary-sprites
```

Build atlas from SVG rectangle markers:
```sh
ruby ../promobu/svg_rect_sprite.rb sf-central-tower.sprite.svg --out-dir . --output-base sf-central-tower-sprites
```

Use atlas textures in rule YAML:
```yml
textures:
	window_atlas:
		type: sprite
		file: sf-central-tower-sprites.webp
		sprites: sf-central-tower-sprites.json
		sprite: level-1-window
```

Notes:
- You can also use `type: adapted` or `type: tiled` with `sprites` + `sprite`.
- Optional `atlas_w` and `atlas_h` can force atlas image dimensions.


## Generate Models

Command format:
```sh
ruby rules.rb <rules-yaml> <width> <height> <depth>
```

Arguments:
- `<rules-yaml>`: rule file under `rules/` (for example `rules/nyc1920.yml`)
- `<width> <height> <depth>`: root box dimensions for the procedural generation

Examples:
```sh
ruby rules.rb rules/canary.yml 5 3 4
ruby rules.rb rules/ttd.yml 10 30 10
ruby rules.rb rules/nyc1920.yml 20 14 8
ruby rules.rb rules/sf-central-tower.yml 10 10 10
```

Output:
- The current generator exports a glTF binary model to `out.glb`.


## Viewer: Build And Run

The viewer is in `viewer/` and uses Three.js.

Install dependencies:
```sh
cd viewer
npm install
```

Run the model preview launcher:
```sh
npm run view -- ../out.glb
```

Other viewer commands:
```sh
npm run dev
npm run build
npm run serve
```
